 vectors ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$  and ${v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ \\sqrt{7} \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "A parametric equation of a plane is given by \n\n$$\nr=p+sb+tc,\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is the position vector of a point on the plane and the vectors $b$ and $c$ are parallel to the plane but not to each other.\n\nHere, the position vector of the given point $M$ is $p=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]$, and the two vectors that are parallel to the plane (but not to each other) are ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$  and ${v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ \\sqrt{7} \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].$\n\nSo, a parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\nr=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]+s[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ \\sqrt{7} \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9736daed-5120-541b-9af8-2423772b6d03"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9736daed-5120-541b-9af8-2423772b6d03" :answer-field/id #uuid "9736daed-5120-541b-9af8-2423772b6d03" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-75d57370-81cc-5500-be9a-c76059ef4dfb" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a70d42f7-d1f2-52ef-9c49-8609198f6893" "answer-43be24cf-8641-5f97-b8d8-732e9a3edde2" "answer-218576bd-e46c-5334-968e-a8f88468df74" "answer-75d57370-81cc-5500-be9a-c76059ef4dfb" "answer-f24ae82e-856b-58e1-b7dd-3cd42518a542"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a70d42f7-d1f2-52ef-9c49-8609198f6893" :answer/id #uuid "a70d42f7-d1f2-52ef-9c49-8609198f6893" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]+s[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ \\sqrt{7} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-43be24cf-8641-5f97-b8d8-732e9a3edde2" :answer/id #uuid "43be24cf-8641-5f97-b8d8-732e9a3edde2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]+s[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ \\sqrt{11} \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-218576bd-e46c-5334-968e-a8f88468df74" :answer/id #uuid "218576bd-e46c-5334-968e-a8f88468df74" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]+s[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -7 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ \\sqrt{7} \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-75d57370-81cc-5500-be9a-c76059ef4dfb" :answer/id #uuid "75d57370-81cc-5500-be9a-c76059ef4dfb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]+s[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ \\sqrt{7} \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f24ae82e-856b-58e1-b7dd-3cd42518a542" :answer/id #uuid "f24ae82e-856b-58e1-b7dd-3cd42518a542" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+s[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ \\sqrt{7} \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-4fcca2b7-695c-58b7-b034-c1fa748f47da" :question/id #uuid "4fcca2b7-695c-58b7-b034-c1fa748f47da" :question/math-academy-id "q-128496" :question/problem "Find a normal vector to the plane\n\n$$\nr=⟨3,-2,1⟩+t⟨2,-5,1⟩+s⟨3,-6,0⟩,\\,t,\\,s\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$" :question/worked-solution "From the parametric equation, we have that $v=⟨2,-5,1⟩$ and $w=⟨3,-6,0⟩$ are parallel to the plane.\n\nNow, we need to find a normal vector of the plane. To do that, we use the cross product of $v$ and $w$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =v\\times w \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\times [\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & -5 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -6 & 0\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =6i+3j+3k \\\\  & =⟨6,3,3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the plane is $n=⟨6,3,3⟩.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-3d97d655-a539-5ca4-b364-2c12300cff27"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3d97d655-a539-5ca4-b364-2c12300cff27" :answer-field/id #uuid "3d97d655-a539-5ca4-b364-2c12300cff27" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-49c23de5-10ac-588e-b906-2f601c3ee4cb" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b3d316ee-8c43-5cbe-ae4e-5f0454d179ef" "answer-3315c99a-bf65-5d24-a5cd-d108af0b9169" "answer-58daaedf-85bc-5389-a9f1-135d9cf2dc54" "answer-49c23de5-10ac-588e-b906-2f601c3ee4cb" "answer-68dd536e-0595-5b7f-bbf4-086bbda96dab"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b3d316ee-8c43-5cbe-ae4e-5f0454d179ef" :answer/id #uuid "b3d316ee-8c43-5cbe-ae4e-5f0454d179ef" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨3,3,3⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3315c99a-bf65-5d24-a5cd-d108af0b9169" :answer/id #uuid "3315c99a-bf65-5d24-a5cd-d108af0b9169" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨3,3,6⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-58daaedf-85bc-5389-a9f1-135d9cf2dc54" :answer/id #uuid "58daaedf-85bc-5389-a9f1-135d9cf2dc54" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨3,6,3⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-49c23de5-10ac-588e-b906-2f601c3ee4cb" :answer/id #uuid "49c23de5-10ac-588e-b906-2f601c3ee4cb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨6,3,3⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-68dd536e-0595-5b7f-bbf4-086bbda96dab" :answer/id #uuid "68dd536e-0595-5b7f-bbf4-086bbda96dab" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨6,6,6⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-59e1275b-72d1-5efa-8072-c2d963838f7f" :question/id #uuid "59e1275b-72d1-5efa-8072-c2d963838f7f" :question/math-academy-id "q-71049" :question/problem "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the points $U(-3,-2,0)$ and $V(1,0,-1)$, and is parallel to the vector $v=⟨-1,5,-1⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find two vectors that are parallel to the plane (but not to each other). We already have one vector $v=⟨-1,5,-1⟩.$ Let's also use the displacement vector $\\overset{\\to }{UV}$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{UV} & =⟨1,0,-1⟩-⟨-3,-2,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4,2,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, if we consider the position vector $u=⟨-3,-2,0⟩$ of the point $U,$ then the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =u+sv+t\\overset{\\to }{UV} \\\\ r & =⟨-3,-2,0⟩+s⟨-1,5,-1⟩+t⟨4,2,-1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-ffaa26fc-cae0-5499-800c-9dd489ee2f5f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ffaa26fc-cae0-5499-800c-9dd489ee2f5f" :answer-field/id #uuid "ffaa26fc-cae0-5499-800c-9dd489ee2f5f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-56c396c7-54c7-56b3-83a2-5e6b3f8f1725" :answer-field/choices ["answer-918bb145-9b81-5373-9e09-80bc4d524835" "answer-c9066316-4e88-5b51-afd6-db0ca189a8ab" "answer-56c396c7-54c7-56b3-83a2-5e6b3f8f1725" "answer-28f06646-216c-5c67-9be6-f9c0e54523f6" "answer-8e59d870-815b-50b7-be77-2034640ef7da"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-918bb145-9b81-5373-9e09-80bc4d524835" :answer/id #uuid "918bb145-9b81-5373-9e09-80bc4d524835" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r=⟨-3,-2,0⟩+s⟨-1,5,-1⟩+t⟨-3,-2,0⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c9066316-4e88-5b51-afd6-db0ca189a8ab" :answer/id #uuid "c9066316-4e88-5b51-afd6-db0ca189a8ab" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r=⟨-3,-2,0⟩+s⟨-1,5,-1⟩+t⟨1,0,-1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-56c396c7-54c7-56b3-83a2-5e6b3f8f1725" :answer/id #uuid "56c396c7-54c7-56b3-83a2-5e6b3f8f1725" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r=⟨-3,-2,0⟩+s⟨-1,5,-1⟩+t⟨4,2,-1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-28f06646-216c-5c67-9be6-f9c0e54523f6" :answer/id #uuid "28f06646-216c-5c67-9be6-f9c0e54523f6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r=⟨-3,-2,0⟩+s⟨-3,-2,0⟩+t⟨1,0,-1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8e59d870-815b-50b7-be77-2034640ef7da" :answer/id #uuid "8e59d870-815b-50b7-be77-2034640ef7da" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The plane is undefined" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186121051 :tutorial/content "Any plane can be uniquely determined by a point and two non-parallel direction vectors. For example, let $\\Pi$ be the plane that passes through the point $P(1,0,2)$ and is parallel to the vectors $\\mathbf{b}= \\langle 0,3,0 \\rangle$  and $\\mathbf{c}= \\langle -1,1,1 \\rangle.$\n\n![](images/ea/ea4ce822abec2b68d2471a2787f4e045493ca43c1c6795a7e0069de80cb5adee.png)\n\nUsing the vectors $\\mathbf{b}$ and $\\mathbf{c},$ we can construct a **parametric equation** of the plane.\n\nFirst, let $R$ be any general point in the plane, with position vector $\\mathbf{r}.$ Notice that we can get from $P$ to $R$ using a linear combination of $\\mathbf{b}$ and $\\mathbf{c}$ with some (unknown for us) coefficients $s$ and $t$, as shown below.\n\n![](images/b4/b40f91c3d75f092c7b29f19770364e7518d37b64ba594a311a762ad79a950e4f.png)\n\nSo, we can write the **parametric equation** of the plane as\n\n$$\n{\\color{red}\\mathbf{r}} = \\mathbf{p}+s{\\color{blue}\\,\\mathbf{b}}+t\\,{\\color{blue}\\mathbf{c}},\n\t\\qquad s,t \\in (-\\infty,\\infty).\n$$\n\nThis formula works whenever $\\mathbf{b}$ and $\\mathbf{c}$ are not parallel.\n\nIn our case, $\\mathbf{b}$ and $\\mathbf{c}$ are indeed not parallel to each other. So, using column vector notation, the parametric equation for the plane $\\Pi$ is given by\n![](images/0d/0d40f8f87e1ed3f3bf5040e925e545169f5528f32cf8dd0052375aa560cc1381.svg)" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186120017 :activity/expected-seconds 660.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
